{"kind":"mount-dora-lidar-crowns","version":3,"inputs":{"lidar":{"file":"maps/mount-dora/reference/lidar/source.json","sha256":"e9712f29c3b1f637e8c1742a95ed40f0321748e023b9b7fed8d2dda664586e4f"},"features":{"file":"maps/mount-dora/features.json","sha256OfFieldsRead":"facf21e6262a1f37be37b79c2b2818919c7937783d488db7e106de16732a5215","fields":"OSM-sourced features only: id, category, tags, geographicGeometry (else geometry); nativeSectors for buildings; authoredStructures ids and geographicGeometry (else geometry)"}},"policy":"Public-domain USGS 3DEP lidar, flown in December 2018. Each crown is canopy the lidar saw that reads as a tree; a few are roofs or thickets these rules cannot tell from one (docs/maps/mount-dora/grid-shapes-followups.md lists the known ones). build-mount-dora.py plants one tree in each crown its seeded greenery leaves empty; nothing here edits the sectors or the art kit.","collection":{"dataset":"FL_Peninsular_Lake_2018","acquired":["2018-12-06","2018-12-06"]},"method":{"rules":{"cellM":0.5,"tallM":2.5,"prominenceM":2,"maxAreaM2":400,"minAreaM2":4,"minWidthM":1.5,"minMultiShare":0.1,"topM":2,"roofShare":0.15},"canopy":"The highest unclassified (class 1) return over the bare earth in each 0.5 m cell, where it stands 2.5 m or more above it and the cell holds no building (class 6) return. This vendor classes no vegetation, so wires, poles, signs and roofs it left unclassified are among it.","crowns":"Each canopy cell climbs a 3 x 3 mean of the canopy to the top it reaches. Neighbouring tops are one crown unless the lower stands 2 m above the saddle between them, merged highest saddle first and never into a crown over 400 m². A crown under 4 m² or under 1.5 m across (four standard deviations along its minor axis) is dropped.","foliage":"A crown is kept only where at least 10% of its canopy returns (unclassified, 2.5 m or more up) came from pulses that returned more than once: foliage lets a pulse through, a wire, pole, sign or roof left unclassified stops it. multiShare records each crown's share and topShare that of the canopy returns within 2 m of its top (null where none stands there); notFoliage lists the crowns the rule drops.","roofs":"A crown centred inside an outline the game draws (OSM and county buildings, the generator's structures) whose top stops the scanner (topShare under 10%) and which as a whole reads under 15% is that building's roof, left unclassified; a tree overhanging a roof lets the scanner through across its crown. roofTops lists them.","frame":"Town metres in the OSM frame: the lidar position minus the outline registration of lidar-roofs.json (-0.04, 0.84) m, which features.json's OSM outlines set."},"metrics":{"crowns":6968,"notFoliage":188,"roofTops":1,"canopyAreaHa":86.68,"multiShare":{"p10":0.239,"p50":0.427},"heightM":{"p10":5.92,"p50":13.17,"p90":19.39},"widthM":{"p10":2.93,"p50":7.94,"p90":18.07}},"columns":["topX","topY","centreX","centreY","areaM2","heightM","widthM","multiShare","topShare"],"crowns":[[48.29,-0.59,47.68,-0.04,7,7.78,2.63,0.402,0.429],[74.79,-0.59,75.33,4.84,63.75,8.6,8.46,0.318,0.365],[107.79,-0.59,107.06,0.18,9.25,4.21,2.67,0.565,0.664],[192.29,-0.59,196.6,2.84,90.5,18.06,8.87,0.471,0.393],[245.29,-0.59,245.29,0.18,6.5,7.76,2.53,0.222,0.202],[288.29,-0.59,285.46,2.79,100,10.04,9.38,0.277,0.295],[302.79,-0.59,302.78,0.9,24.5,15.38,4.76,0.384,0.216],[316.79,-0.59,316.82,1.53,48.5,15.6,6.16,0.441,0.589],[333.79,-0.59,332.23,1.03,36.75,14.33,4.91,0.592,0.703],[356.79,-0.59,359.17,3.91,114.75,10.61,9.98,0.258,0.331],[479.29,-0.59,478.09,6.25,157,11.39,10.92,0.382,0.541],[535.79,-0.59,533.27,0.37,20.5,15.24,3.07,0.442,0.415],[668.79,-0.59,665.56,3.46,100.25,13.12,10.8,0.404,0.661],[839.79,-0.59,837.7,9.15,330.75,18.64,19.58,0.44,0.506],[873.79,-0.59,873.48,0.54,11.25,16.38,3.34,0.363,0.353],[984.29,-0.59,985.91,1.08,24.25,9.88,5.16,0.333,0.248],[1048.29,-0.59,1050.19,1.59,74.5,13.05,6.13,0.568,0.602],[1193.29,-0.59,1188.61,1.9,44.75,14.94,6.5,0.398,0.477],[1403.79,